\title{CUDA Hierarchy}

\p{Grid: Top-level define how many blocks are needed to cover the computation across [SMs](OGCS6).}
\p{Block: Ensures all warps in a block are resident on the same [SM](OGCS6) and have the same [shared memory](8GZN).}
\p{Warp: A group of 32 threads that execute the same instruction.}
\p{Thread: A single thread within a warp.}

